.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt BSDDD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsddd
.Nd experimental BSD desktop session compatibility daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl Fl probe
.Nm
.Fl Fl foreground
.Oo Fl Fl power-group Ar name | Fl Fl power-group-file Ar path Oc
.Nm
.Fl Fl check-owner Ar pid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
BSD cubed is a BSD-licensed desktop compatibility project for
.Fx .
This version supplies session discovery and controller lifetime
management through ConsoleKit2.
It does not yet enable a native GNOME Wayland login.
.Pp
The
.Fl Fl probe
option queries the existing ConsoleKit service without acquiring a bus name.
It requires neither root nor a desktop session.
.Pp
The
.Fl Fl foreground
option runs a partial
.Dq org.freedesktop.login1
service on the system bus.
It does not replace or queue behind an existing owner.
Bus policy must explicitly permit the caller to own that name.
The FreeBSD port installs a disabled-by-default rc.d service and a policy
permitting only root to own the name.
The service uses daemon(8) and rc.subr.
Enable it only for controlled integration until device/VT behavior is verified.
.Pp
The
.Fl Fl check-owner
option checks that the bus name belongs to the specified positive process ID.
It is read-only and fails if identity cannot be verified.
Service readiness does not assert that a session or desktop is usable.
.Pp
The service implements GetSession, GetSessionByPID, ListSessions,
and the read-only session properties Id, Active, Type, Class and State.
TakeControl requires the original D-Bus peer to own and belong to the session.
ReleaseControl is restricted to that controlling connection.
Each controller uses a separate backend connection, which is closed on client
disconnect, backend restart, release failure or daemon shutdown.
Forced takeover is unsupported.
.Pp
Experimental TakeDevice, ReleaseDevice, PauseDeviceComplete and unicast
pause/resume notifications preserve backend device descriptors.
Their protocol tests do not prove real DRM/input revocation or VT switching.
.Pp
The partial Seat interface forwards SwitchTo only for the active controlling
connection belonging to that seat. ConsoleKit and the kernel validate the target
VT; physical console switching and recovery remain unverified.
.Pp
Selected Manager power methods and
.Ic Inhibit
are accepted only for the original D-Bus peer.
The methods are
.Ic CanSuspend ,
.Ic CanHibernate ,
.Ic CanHybridSleep ,
.Ic CanPowerOff ,
.Ic CanReboot ,
.Ic CanSuspendThenHibernate ,
.Ic Suspend ,
.Ic Hibernate ,
.Ic HybridSleep ,
.Ic PowerOff ,
.Ic Reboot
and
.Ic Inhibit .
Bus policy lets any user send to the name; that is not authorization.
.Pp
The peer must satisfy every one of the following.
The system bus must report the peer's uid and process id.
Uid 0 is refused, as is a call on the daemon's own bus connection.
PolicyKit would treat uid 0 as authorized; this daemon does not.
The process must own an active, local ConsoleKit session.
The uid must be a member of the power group.
PolicyKit
.Ic CheckAuthorization
must return authorized for subject kind
.Dq system-bus-name ,
using that peer's unique name and with user interaction disabled.
A challenge, a missing authority, a bad subject, or any lookup error is a denial.
.Pp
The default power group is
.Sy operator ,
the FreeBSD group historically permitted to shut the system down.
Set
.Va bsddd_power_group
in
.Xr rc.conf 5
to another single group name.
The rc.d script passes it as
.Fl Fl power-group .
An empty or illegal name prevents the service from starting.
.Fl Fl power-group-file
re-reads one line of the form
.Ql power_group="name"
on each call and fails closed when the file is missing or malformed.
It is not combined with
.Fl Fl power-group .
.Pp
.Ic Can*
answers reflect that caller.
A denied caller receives
.Dq no ,
including for
.Ic CanSuspendThenHibernate ,
even when ConsoleKit would report
.Dq na
or
.Dq yes
to root.
An authorized caller receives
.Dq yes
or
.Dq na
from ConsoleKit's capability reply.
.Dq challenge
and any other capability reply become
.Dq no .
If the authority or the capability lookup fails, the call returns an access error
rather than
.Dq yes .
.Ic SuspendThenHibernate
is not implemented and stays
.Dq na
for an authorized caller.
.Pp
Only after the decision is allow does the daemon ask ConsoleKit to perform
.Ic Suspend ,
.Ic Hibernate ,
.Ic HybridSleep ,
.Ic Stop ,
.Ic Restart
or
.Ic Inhibit .
ConsoleKit then sees this daemon's connection, so that call is actuation, not
the caller's authorization.
.Ic PrepareForSleep
is emitted around an attempted sleep or power action, not around a denial.
.Ic Inhibit
accepts modes
.Dq block
and
.Dq delay
and uses the same decision with action
.Dq org.freedesktop.login1.inhibit .
The inhibitor is held on the daemon's ConsoleKit connection, so only one login1
inhibitor is available at a time.
A successful reply is not verified hardware suspend or power-off.
.Pp
The port installs a PolicyKit action file whose defaults are
.Dq no ,
and a rule that returns yes for the
.Sy operator
group and no for
.Dq root .
Keep that rule aligned with
.Va bsddd_power_group .
If they name different groups, the call stays denied.
.Pp
It does not implement session creation, a complete Seat/User model,
interactive PolicyKit prompts, or a user service manager.
Consumers must not interpret the presence of the bus name
as full logind support.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
.It Ev DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
Overrides the system bus address as provided by GLib.
The tests direct this to a private bus; do not set it for privileged deployment.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error returns 64.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.bsd3.login1.rules"
.It Pa /usr/local/share/polkit-1/actions/org.bsd3.login1.policy
Action definitions for the login1 power and inhibit ids.
Defaults deny every subject.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.bsd3.login1.rules
Shipped authority rule for the operator group.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Denis Lemire Aq Mt denis@lemire.name
